WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.236
-My first guest is an Emmy-
and Oscar-nominated actor.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.971
You can see her
in the highly anticipated

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:07.673
new movie "Wonder Woman 1984,"

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:11.043
which will be in select theaters
and IMAX Christmas Day,

00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:14.981
and it will be available
the same day on HBO Max.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.584
She is also hosting
"Saturday Night Live"

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.787
this weekend,
with musical guest Dua Lipa.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.389
Please welcome Kristen Wiig!

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:24.924
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:29.061
♪ Kristen Wiig,
nice to meet ya ♪

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:33.366
♪ We're gonna see you
play the Cheetah ♪

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:37.237
♪ Kristen Wiig-cha,
nice to meetcha ♪

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:41.607
♪ You can watch at home
or in theaters ♪

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:45.578
♪ Kristen Wiig,
nice to meet ya ♪

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:48.715
-Look at that -- Kristen Wiig!
Come on.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.416
-Oh, my God.
-You look fantastic.

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.618
I miss seeing you.
I'm so thankful,

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:55.755
and I'm so happy you're here.
-I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.656
-You look great, bud.
I want to get into "SNL"

00:00:57.656 --> 00:00:59.125
and everything.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.295
I just want to say thank you for
helping us out over the summer.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.764
We did the sketch called
"The Longest Days of Our Lives."

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.966
-That was so fun.
-I laughed so hard

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.969
just even filming --
just filming it.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.872
Nancy, by the way,
who clearly loves you,

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.941
didn't even get a chance
to even say hi.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:17.109
But she was seeing everything.
I wasn't.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:20.513
She was holding the iPad this
way, so she was going like...

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.248
[ Laughing ]

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.584
And you and Will were going --
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.086
You and Will were --
-It was so fun.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:28.921
Needed it, yeah.
-It was fantastic.

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:31.925
And I love that
you had your own wigs.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:37.130
-Well, I have a costume wig...
-Box?

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:40.033
-It's a big box, yeah.
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:43.903
Well, you never know when you're
gonna need, like, a wig.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.738
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.373
A funny costume.
-That's true.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:50.843
-Yeah, our friend's daughter
had a birthday,

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.244
and we did, like, a drive-by,
and we're like,

00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:56.448
"Well, we should probably wear
wigs and costumes."

00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:57.783
-Even though
they didn't ask you at all?

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.152
-They didn't ask us.
-No, of course not.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.553
Yeah, but you wore them.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:04.023
-You're hosting "SNL" this week.
It's the Christmas episode.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.258
It's my favorite episode
of the year.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.893
-It's my favorite.
My favorite probably

00:02:07.893 --> 00:02:10.863
was when you hosted --

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:12.331
It was the first time you
hosted, I think?

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:14.000
The Christmas show.
-Yeah. Yeah, that's right.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.235
That was, like,
one of my favorite --

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.036
-Where we all danced?
-Yes, the monologue

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.705
where we all danced
around the studio.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.340
-Oh, man.
Wasn't that so much fun?

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.574
And it was snowing.
-It was so fun.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.310
-Fake snow was coming down.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.112
-Tiny little bits of plastic.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.280
-Yeah.
-Before any sketch.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.249
-And we're like, "Ahh."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:33.886
-Before any sketches.
Before "SNL,"

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:35.855
I think I know a little bit
about your background.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.891
Groundlings before that?
Were you in plays?

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.292
Were you doing --
-Um...

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:45.865
I mean, I did, like, a couple
school plays but in the chorus.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.566
-Okay.
-Like, the people that audition

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:50.136
that don't get the parts,
then those were the parts --

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:51.637
That's what I did.
-You did that?

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:54.106
-I did the chorus parts.
-And were you good at that?

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:56.442
-No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.678
No.
But it was like --

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.047
It was "Anything Goes,"
so I was like --

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:06.252
I, like, danced and tapped.
I had never tap-danced before.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.320
[ Laughter ]
We didn't have phones back then.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.922
-They didn't even
ask you to tap.

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:12.358
You're like, "I got this."
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.726
I know, exactly.
I just tapped across the stage

00:03:14.726 --> 00:03:17.096
in the middle of a scene.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.964
Yeah, I remember my mom
came to see the play,

00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:21.434
and I waved to her
from the thing.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.770
-Aww.
-Yeah, and she's like,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.970
you're not --
-So cute.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.305
-Yeah, but no,
I wasn't like 8 years old.

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:28.774
This was, like, high school.
-Oh.

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:31.311
[ Laughter ]
Waving at your mom?

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.644
-No, I was, like,
fully in high school.

00:03:32.644 --> 00:03:35.514
-"Hey, Mom!" -- Your voice
was even deeper back then.

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:37.483
-Waah!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.551
-Look at you now.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.586
Now you're in
"Wonder Woman 1984."

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:41.787
-It's crazy.
-Wait.

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.756
I want to hear everything
about this.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.791
-Yeah, I still --
Like, I just wanted to come out

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:48.161
because I feel like
it didn't happen.

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.362
It's like a dream.
-Right?

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.698
You were in a major
superhero movie.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:54.633
Like, this is major.
I'm so excited.

00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:55.868
What was it like?

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.638
Did you do, like,
the workouts all day?

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:02.341
-Yeah, no, I know.
It was -- It was --

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:03.910
I mean,
I knew I would have to train,

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.412
'cause I started training
before I left.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.848
They got me a trainer like
a month before,

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.717
and it was like, you know,
train for like an hour,

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.185
like, then you're good,
and then I got there,

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:14.487
and it was like --
-Special weights and...?

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:17.557
-Oh, no, it was like --
Oh, you train for hour,

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:21.560
and then, you have stunt
choreography for four hours,

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.195
and then you have lunch,
and then you have

00:04:23.195 --> 00:04:25.431
a movement class,
and then, like --

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:29.235
-Really?
-Yeah, it was very, um...

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:30.269
intense.
-It's work, man.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.538
-No, it was great.
It was amazing.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.507
-How did you get involved
with this?

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.675
Did you know they wanted you
for the sequel?

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:39.445
-I g-- I guess, like,

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:44.584
Patty, yeah, she reached out
to my --

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:47.886
My agent called me and said,
"You know, Patty Jenkins

00:04:47.886 --> 00:04:50.923
wants to talk to you."
And I was like, "Yeah."

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.225
-It's awesome.
-I was like, "Yes.

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:54.494
Could this be
the 'Wonder Woman' sequel?"

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:56.696
So they didn't know.
Like, my agents didn't know,

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:59.765
and I wasn't allowed
to tell them anything.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:02.801
-After the meeting?
-Yeah, I had to sign something

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.570
before I even, like,
talked to anyone.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:05.938
And I am a nerd.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.873
Like, I take that stuff
really seriously.

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:10.976
-Yeah, you could get arrested.
-I was like, "I can't tell you.

00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:13.979
It's a part, but I am not
allowed to tell you what it is."

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:15.280
-And you're doing this
while you're driving,

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:16.916
not even looking at the road.
-Yes, yes.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.285
-"And I can't tell you
where it is, and, uh --"

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.553
"Look at the road, Kristen!
Look at the road!

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.020
You're driving."
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.856
-That's wild.
So then, you met with her,

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.625
and she said,
"We'd like you for this?"

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:27.760
-Well, I had to go do, like,

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.696
a screen-test reading thing
in London.

00:05:30.696 --> 00:05:32.598
So I had to, like,
fly to London.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.400
And even my friends, I'm like,
"I'm going to London.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.337
I can't discuss anything.
I can't tell you why I'm going."

00:05:38.337 --> 00:05:40.439
-"Kristen, you're on a Jet-ski!"

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:43.743
"I guess I can't
say anything -- Whoa!"

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.478
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:48.013
-I get paranoid
that the Warner Bros. police

00:05:48.013 --> 00:05:49.449
are gonna...
-Are gonna arrest you.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.417
-Yeah, were gonna arrest me.
-Who do you play in the movie?

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.519
What can we say
without spoiling anything?

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:54.853
-I'm so scared.
-I know.

00:05:54.853 --> 00:05:58.290
Am I allowed to say anything?
-I'm playing Cheetah.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.493
-I mean, first of all,
I love Cheetah, by the way.

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:02.027
I think it's perfect.
I love it.

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:05.798
-She starts off very
as Diana's friend.

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:08.033
-Yep.
-And she's very shy and awkward,

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:11.570
and then, later becomes --
-Yeah, that's all you can say.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.972
I don't want to --
Look at you.

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:15.808
You're really good.
You're freaki--

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:19.011
You're crying blood.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:20.178
I don't want
to ruin anything, either,

00:06:20.178 --> 00:06:21.714
so don't say any more.

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:23.549
Dude, you do
crazy stunts and action.

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:25.484
Like, I don't even know
what's you in there.

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:28.554
I know you as Kristen Wiig.
I mean, you're so funny,

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.523
and you're just awesome in
everything, I just love you.

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:32.992
But this was a totally --
Like, dude, you kick butt

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:35.961
in this, you and Wonder Woman.
Oh, it's fantastic.

00:06:35.961 --> 00:06:37.162
-It was really fun.

00:06:37.162 --> 00:06:38.831
-Do you know how to do stunts
now and stuff?

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:41.633
-I mean, we --
There was a lot of, like --

00:06:41.633 --> 00:06:43.569
Yeah, there was
a lot of training.

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:46.104
I mean, I'm not like --
-If I name a stunt,

00:06:46.104 --> 00:06:49.741
could you tell me what it is?
-Oh, sure.

00:06:49.741 --> 00:06:52.911
-How about deck the halls?
-Yep...that --

00:06:52.911 --> 00:06:56.782
that --
that is a lot of arms.

00:06:56.782 --> 00:06:59.719
-Yep.
2/3 Nelson?

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:01.854
-Oh, boy, that's an oldie.
-Okay.

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.121
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.121 --> 00:07:07.993
How about the --
the lobster punch?

00:07:07.993 --> 00:07:09.595
-The lobster punch.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:12.164
That's only been done
a couple times.

00:07:12.164 --> 00:07:14.199
-Well, this is amazing stuff,
for anyone watching.

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:15.601
-Yeah, the lobster punch
is hard.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:19.272
It's more of a claw action.
-Than a punch? Oh.

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:20.873
-Than a punch.
Well, it's, like, together.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:22.842
So it's really hard.
That's why they rarely do it.

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:24.410
-They described it well then,
yeah.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.312
A lobster punch.

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:28.948
The Chattanooga Choo-Choo?
-Oh, yeah.

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:31.383
From the '30s.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.383 --> 00:07:33.552
Oh, really? The 1930s?
♪♪

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:36.421
-Oh, wait.
You sneak up on your opponent

00:07:36.421 --> 00:07:39.525
like this.
[ Both laugh ]

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:41.727
-You square up to your opponent,
and you tap-dance --

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:43.295
-And you hit them on the head
with a tambourine.

00:07:43.295 --> 00:07:45.698
-[ Laughs ]
-No, I don't know.

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:47.633
-I want to show everyone
a clip from the movie.

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:50.502
Here is Kristen Wiig
in "Wonder Woman 1984."

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:52.638
Take a look at this.

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.540
-Do you know that song?
-No, no.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.707
-Hey, Jake.

00:07:55.707 --> 00:07:58.243
Jake, hi, can you...

00:07:58.243 --> 00:08:01.714
-I had a convertible.
Anyway...

00:08:01.714 --> 00:08:03.949
-Hi. [ Chuckles ]
I know, walk much?

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:06.318
The latch of my --
Oh.

00:08:06.318 --> 00:08:09.021
♪♪

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:10.655
-Good morning.

00:08:10.655 --> 00:08:12.858
-Hi.
Thank you.

00:08:12.858 --> 00:08:16.462
-Diana Prince, cultural
anthropology and archaeology.

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:19.064
-Barbara Minerva,
geology, gemology, lithology,

00:08:19.064 --> 00:08:20.833
and part-time cryptozoologist.

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:26.438
-Oh, wow.
-Kept busy in college.

00:08:26.438 --> 00:08:28.173
Sorry.
It's these heels, you know.

00:08:28.173 --> 00:08:29.375
I -- Just stupid.

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:30.576
I don't know why
I was gonna wear heels.

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:33.078
Scientists don't wear heels.
-Sometimes we do.

00:08:33.078 --> 00:08:34.714
-Right.
Right.

00:08:34.714 --> 00:08:36.615
-Have a nice day.
-Those are cool.

00:08:36.615 --> 00:08:39.084
I like those, the animal print.
Rarr.

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:40.886
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:40.886 --> 00:08:43.655
-Oh!
Aaah!

00:08:43.655 --> 00:08:46.125
-"Wonder Woman 1984"
will be in select theaters

00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:50.062
and IMAX on Christmas Day!
What a Christmas present.

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:52.565
And will be available
at the same day on HBO Max.

